The Rust binding gives you typed `Session`, `Reference`, and `Argument` over the
pancake archives
([`lib.rs`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/bindings/rust/src/lib.rs)).
Cargo features select transports (`tcp` and `inproc` by default, `iroh`
opt-in). The package is not published yet; start from the
[checkout instructions]($link.page('bindings')).

## The same round-trip

The [Start building]($link.page('start')) round-trip (connect, fetch, send,
handle the reply) reads like this in Rust. The snippet uses the crate's opt-in
`async` feature and runs inside a `tokio::task::LocalSet`. `connect` starts the
inbound loop itself, so `serve` is only for awaiting shutdown.

> []($block.attrs('code-tabs'))
> **tcp**
> ```rust
> use pancake::{connect, tcp_locator, Argument};
>
> // Plain TCP uses a cleartext host and port.
> let partner = tcp_locator("127.0.0.1", 9099);
>
> let session = connect(&partner, None, None).await?;
> let greeter = session.fetch("greeter").await?; // a capability, by name
> match session
>     .send(&greeter, "greet", &[Argument::String("world".into())])
>     .await
> {
>     Ok(Argument::String(reply)) => println!("{reply}"),
>     Ok(other) => println!("unexpected reply: {other:?}"),
>     Err(reason) => eprintln!("the greeter refused: {reason:?}"),
> }
> session.close();
> ```
> **iroh**
> ```rust
> // Cargo.toml: pancake = { …, features = ["iroh"] }
> use pancake::{connect, Argument, Reachability};
>
> // Discovery resolves a bare iroh node ID without an address hint.
> let partner = "ocapn://3b6a…da29.iroh";
>
> let session = connect(partner, Some(Reachability::Discovery), None).await?;
> let greeter = session.fetch("greeter").await?; // a capability, by name
> match session
>     .send(&greeter, "greet", &[Argument::String("world".into())])
>     .await
> {
>     Ok(Argument::String(reply)) => println!("{reply}"),
>     Ok(other) => println!("unexpected reply: {other:?}"),
>     Err(reason) => eprintln!("the greeter refused: {reason:?}"),
> }
> session.close();
> ```

The iroh tab needs the `iroh` Cargo feature and a discovery-reachable node id.
The session calls stay the same.

## Async

Async rides [tokio](https://tokio.rs/) behind an opt-in `async` feature. Handles
are `!Send`, so each lives on one task inside a `LocalSet`. Only the socket
reads and writes await; the protocol verbs never block. To host the other half,
`listen` binds a `Server` whose `accept` yields a `Session` per partner.

## Actors

`session.spawn` and `session.publish` take a `FnMut(&str, &[Argument])` closure
returning `Result<Argument, String>`. An `Err` breaks the answer with its words,
and a panic settles it broken without crossing the C boundary.
[Concepts]($link.page('concepts')) covers pipelining and attenuation.

The full surface lives in the
[Rust binding README](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/bindings/rust/README.md),
and the
[rooms chat client](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/apps/rooms/clients/rust/client.rs)
is the biggest real program on this surface.
